Similarities and AbstractionThe FIN-Bench similarities/abstraction task probes models’ ability to
identify shared properties or abstract relations between two words. Given a word pair, the model must
explain what they have in common or pick the best description of their similarity. We provide acloze
formulation(CF), where the model freely describes the relation, and amultiple-choice formulation(MCF),
where it selects the most appropriate explanation from a small set of options. This subset contains 76
examples.
