W ′Tn =W+ (XY ⊤)Tn (4)
Once these matrices are trained independently for various tasks (e.g. domains or styles),
we can perform interactive model adaptations through a calibrated linear combination of
multiple LoRA matrices1, akin to a simplified Mixture of LoRA Experts (MoLE) but with-
out a gating network, aiming to enhance the usability and to be able to interactively bias
the model’s knowledge along desired dimensions without the need for fine-tuning. Unlike
traditional MoEs that rely on networks to weigh contributions, we allow domain-specific co-
efficients and a user scaling factor (α) for fine-grained control. Consequently, the adaptation
is defined as follows:
