A.1 F1(·,·)
For each character positioni∈ {1, . . . , L}, letmi =I[i∈E maj]andn i =I[i∈E min]indicate
whether the character is covered by a major or minor error span. We write(m ic, nic)and(m is, nis)for
the candidate annotationE c and the support/reference annotationE s, respectively. The character-level
true-positive credit isc i = max(βmicmis, βnicnis, γmicnis, γnicmis), whereβandγare the exact-severity
and cross-severity credit weights, withβ > γ≥0. LetC= PLi=1 ci andS(E) = PLi=1 max(mi, ni).
