3.4 Backtranslation
Backtranslation (BT) is implemented by first using
a pretrained model (Japanese → English) on the
available parallel data as shown in Figure 2. Using
this model, synthetic English sentences are gener-
ated from monolingual Japanese corpora. These
synthetic pairs are then added to the original paral-
lel dataset, effectively enlarging the training corpus.
This augmentation proved crucial in mitigating data
scarcity, providing additional coverage for domain-
specific and colloquial expressions.
