22 According to Butler (2003), t he usage of a sequence of words in a single integrated model in Machine 
Translation refers to the approach of modeling translations as a sequence of words or tokens within a unified 
framework. This approach allows the translation system to generate translations one word at a time, considering 
the context and dependencies between words in  the source and target languages. In traditional Machine 
Translation systems, the translation process was often divided into separate stages, such as word alignment, phrase 
extraction, and reordering. However, with the advent of neural Machine Translation  (NMT) and sequence -to-
sequence models, a single integrated model can be used to handle the entire translation process.  
