the MT model. Our results in Table 4 suggest that
TransAlign does not depend on itsowntranslations.
The performance improvements obtained by label
projection with TransAlign are orthogonal to gains
obtained by higher translation quality.
E Further Analysis: Language Coverage
NLLB has seen substantially more languages in
pretraining than LaBSE (200 vs. 109 languages).
To ensure that performance improvements obtained
by TransAlign do not simply stem from broader
language coverage, we evaluate TransAlign and Ac-
cAlign on a subset of languages seen in the pretrain-
ing of both models. We observe that TransAlign
still outperforms AccAlign even on a subset of lan-
guages seen by both models (see Table 5).
