5.5 Paraphrasing Experiment
To evaluate how well models generate fluent En­
glish paraphrases of Urdu idioms and sentences
while preserving meaning, we assess seven LLMs
using semantic similarity, surface­level lexical over­
lap, Levenshtein distance, and multilingual embed­
ding coherence. Table 10 presents the results.
Across evaluation metrics, Gemini­3 and GPT­
OSS­20B consistently outperform smaller models.
Gemini­3 achieves the highest lexical alignment
with a ROUGE score of 0.32 and a unigram overlap
of 35.94%, while maintaining top­tier semantic fi­
delity (BERTScore 0.90). Levenshtein distances be­
tween 39 and 43 across all systems suggest substan­
tial rewriting behavior, with Gemini­3 and GPT­
OSS­20B demonstrating the most precise para­
phrasing capabilities. Cross­lingual embedding­
based evaluations using LASER, LaBSE, and mul­
tilingual USE further confirm that Gemini­3 leads
in preserving deep semantic structure (LaBSE 0.59),
whereas smaller models show weaker alignment.
