2 THEORETICALANALYSIS
We now present an analysis suggesting that in the high-error regime (i.e., for translators with rel-
atively low accuracy), observations may be more cost effective than interactive experiments. It is
instructive to consider interaction in supervised learning and how it relates to unsupervised machine
translation. We defer this comparison the the appendix, Section C.
