1 INTRODUCTION
Modern NLP research focuses largely on the languages on the inter-
net, which consists of only 20 of the 7,000 languages of the world
[6]. This leaves the majority of languages understudied, which are
also referred to as low-resource languages (LRLs), and are spoken
by a large section of world population. LRLs can be described as
