H. Win Margin
To compare two systems, we define awinwhen
the difference inBLEUscores between the alter-
native system and the baseline system exceeds a
threshold of 5 points. Formally, lets(A)i and s(B)i
denote theBLEUscores for source textifrom the
alternative systemA and the baseline systemB,
respectively. Thedeltais computed as:
∆i =s (A)i −s (B)i .
We define a win as∆i > 1, and a loss as∆i <− 1.
Tiesornegligibledifferences( |∆i| ≤5)areignored.
Thewin rate marginis then computed as:
WinMargin= 100· Nwins −N losses
Nvalid
where Nwins is the number of instances with∆i >
5, Nlosses is the number of instances with∆i <
−5, and Nvalid = Nwins + Nlosses is the number of
comparisons where a win or loss occurred.
To analyze performance with respect to length,
we group the source text intoQ quantiles based
on their token length and report the win margin per
quantile.
