B.7 MTTRACES GENERATED BY PROMPTING STRATEGIES AS INTERMEDIATE TOKENS:
WHAT HAPPENS WHEN WE CHANGE THE TEACHER?
We run additional information on Xhosa and change the teacher from
Llama-4-Scout-17B-16E-Instructtogemma-3-27b-it. GEMMA’s performance
zero-shot MT performance (on FLORES 200, BLEU=12.82, MetricX=7.62) is worse than
LLAMA’s (BLEU=16.90, MetricX=6.53) and we want to investigate how this impacts our
findings. First of all, COTFT outperforms IOFT across prompting strategies with the excep-
tion of SBYS. IOFT-MAXoutperforms IOFT and we observe the same behaviour between
IOFT-MAX(COMPTRA) and IOFT as we did with LLAMA. Despite COTFT with SBYS
underperforming IOFT, IOFT-MAX(SBYS) outperforms IOFT, meaning that translation attempts
embedded in SBYS-inspired CoT are helpful, but they are drowned out by other useless tokens,
which impacts how well COTFT performs. Ultimately, IOFT-BOA works best; although IOFT-
MAX(TEAR) achieves higher BLEU scores it lags behind in terms of MetricX. It even outperforms
the teachergemma-3-27b-itdespite being six times smaller.
