We further analyze the performance of AgentE-
val across different backbone models under both
the multi-agent (“Debate-”) and single-agent con-
figurations. To complement the correlation anal-
ysis in the previous subsection, we employ mul-
tiple agreement-based measures: Simple Agree-
ment( the proportion of cases where annotators
give exactly the same labels), Cohen’s κ (Cohen,
1960), Linear/Quadratic Weighted κ (Yilmaz and
Demirhan, 2023), ICC(3,1) (Shrout and Fleiss,
