C Evaluation Results and Thinking
Token Statistics of DRT Models on
Literary Translation Tasks
Tables 7- 10 present the performance of the DRT
models across three literary translation benchmarks
with respect to the GEA100, GEA5, GRB, and GRF
metrics, respectively. Table 11 shows the token
statistics under different budgets. Figure 6 visual-
izes DRT models’ translation quality (GRB&GRF
score, right y-axis) and the actual number of
thinking tokens (left y-axis). On the in-domain
MetaphorTrans task, there is a positive growth of
the quality scores as the thinking budget increases
to around 300 tokens, then the score generally stabi-
lizes. While on the other two out-of-domain tasks,
the performance fluctuates and shows an overall
downward trend as thinking tokens increase.
