TreePrompt: Leveraging Hierarchical Few-Shot Example Selection for Improved English-Persian and English-German Translation,"TreePrompt: Leveraging Hierarchical Few-Shot Example Selection for
Improved English-Persian and English-German Translation
Ramtin Kakavand, Ebrahim Ansari
Department of Computer Science
Institute for Advanced Studies in Basic Sciences
Zanjan, Iran
{r.kakavand, ansari}@iasbs.ac.ir
Abstract
Large Language Models (LLMs) have consis-
tently demonstrated strong performance in ma-
chine translation, especially when guided by
high-quality prompts. Few-shot prompting is
an effective technique to improve translation
quality; however, most existing example selec-
tion methods focus solely on query-to-example
similarity and do not account for the quality of
the examples. In this work, we propose TreeP-
rompt, a novel example selection approach
that learns LLM preferences to identify high-
quality, contextually relevant examples within
a tree-structured framework. To further ex-
plore the balance between similarity and qual-
ity, we combine TreePrompt with K-Nearest
Neighbors (K-NN) and Adaptive Few-Shot
Prompting (AFSP). Evaluations on two lan-
guage pairs—English–Persian (MIZAN) and
English–German (WMT19)—show that inte-
grating TreePrompt with AFSP or Random se-
lection leads to improved translation perfor-
mance.
1 Introduction
Large language models (LLMs) demonstrate re-
markable capabilities in machine translation (MT)
tasks(Bawden and Yvon, 2023). Significant ad-
vancements have been made in these models, par-
ticularly with architectures such as ChatGPT and
GPT-4 (Ouyang et al., 2022; Hendy et al., 2023;
Zhang et al., 2023b).
Few-shot prompting plays a crucial role in
improving translation quality and enhancing a
model’s ability to generalize with limited data (Vi-
lar et al., 2023; Chen et al., 2023). By selecting ap-
propriate examples, we can effectively unlock the
translation potential of LLMs (Tang et al., 2025).
Although numerous example selection strategies
have been proposed, most primarily focus on the
similarity between the examples and the input
query.
