3.4 Monetary Cost of Benchmark Construction
ϵ-greedy consistently outperforms brute search at every budget level (Table 2): for only $104, it
achieves top-10 difficulty of 19.7, which brute search cannot reach even at $10,403, a 100 × cost
reduction. Performance beyond our actual budget is estimated synthetically (Figures 4 and 5). A
detailed token-level cost breakdown is provided in Appendix I.
While our pipeline uses Gemini-2.5-Pro as the difficulty estimator ($1.25/1M input and $10.00/1M
output tokens), the framework is estimator-agnostic: the quality estimation component can be replaced
with cheaper alternatives such as learned regression models (e.g., MetricX, COMET) or source-only
difficulty predictors [5], reducing per-query cost while retaining the same MAB search framework.
