cates that a model ranks itself more favorably than
its peers do. The consistently negative diagonal
scores confirm thatthese models systematically
favor their own outputsacross four language
directions—except Gemini on Kurdish→English.
We hypothesize that this exception arises because
Kurdish is a relatively higher-resource language
compared to Bemba, Aymara, and Luo, leading to
more diverse and less model-specific source text
generation (further analyzed in Section 5.2).
