8 Related Work
Automatic Benchmark Creation.As existing
benchmarks become increasingly saturated by
rapid LLM advancements (Glazer et al., 2025), au-
tomatic benchmark construction using LLMs has
gained significant traction (Pombal et al., 2025a).
Methods range from synthesizing test sets via
prompt workflows (Sprague et al., 2024; Zouhar
et al., 2025) to constructing prompts from exist-
ing data (Li et al., 2024; Vergopoulos et al., 2025).
Efficacy is assessed via benchmark agreement (Per-
litz et al., 2024) or ranking correlation with human
benchmarks (Pombal et al., 2025a), using accuracy
for verifiable tasks or LLM judges for open-ended
outputs (Xu et al., 2023; Pombal et al., 2025a). A
key advantage is the ability to generate evaluation
data for arbitrary domains and language pairs on
demand, which is particularly valuable for settings
where human data curation is expensive or difficult.
