A Statistical Significance and Sample Size
Justification
To justify our sample size of N=200, we conduct
a bootstrap analysis on the Bemba→English trans-
lation task under the LLM-as-a-testset and LLM-
as-an-evaluator setup. For each of the three mod-
els (Gemini 2.5 Pro, GPT-4.1, Claude Opus 4),
we construct the 3×3 ranking table and perform
bootstrap resampling (B=10,000) to compute 95%
confidence intervals.
Table 13 reports the mean rankings with standard
deviations, and Table 14 reports the corresponding
95% confidence intervals. The diagonal entries—
representing each model’s ranking of itself—show
no overlap with the off-diagonal entries in the same
column, confirming that each model ranks itself sig-
nificantly higher than the other two. Based on this
analysis and budget constraints, we useN=200 for
all experiments.
