manuscript preparation were conducted independently by the research lab to ensure transparency
and reproducibility. The companies had no role in the study design or the reporting of results. In
addition to these financial interests, TabiBench was curated, standardized, and released by the same
authors who developed TabiBERT and who use TabiBench to evaluate it in this paper; Section 4.5
documents the safeguards that keep the benchmark’s construction independent of this evaluation.
This authorship overlap applies to all authors equally, not only those named above; beyond it and
the financial interests already stated, the authors declare no other competing interests.
Ethics Statement
Ethical approval was not required for this study. It involved no human participants or animal subjects
and collected no personal data; it used existing text corpora and datasets, and the translation-quality
audit was carried out by volunteer annotators who rated published text and are acknowledged by
name with their consent.
Data Availability Statement
TabiBERT’s model weights are available on Hugging Face (Türker et al. 2025c), and its pre-
training and fine-tuning code, training configurations and the per-seed scores of Appendix A.3 on
GitHub (Türker et al. 2025d). TabiBench is released on Hugging Face (Türker et al. 2025b) as a
collection of 27 datasets, each redistributed under the terms of its original source as recorded in
Table 16; MedNLI-TR is excluded for the reasons given in Section 4.5. The translation audit scripts
and anonymized ratings are released with the code. The pretraining corpus is not redistributed,
because portions of it (academic publications and books from institutional repositories) are subject
fhttps://vngrs.com/
ghttps://lambda.ai/
26 Natural Language Processing
to licensing restrictions; its sources, sizes and sampling rates are given in Section 3 and Table 2,
and comparable corpora can be assembled from the publicly available sources listed there.
