A.1 THEORETICALANALYSIS
Below, we provide a theoretical analysis of how calibration error relates to the accuracy of Naïve RAG (NR)
and Agentic RAG (AR).
Denote aNR and eNR as the probabilities of producing a correct or incorrect answer in NR, respectively. Note
that aNR +e NR may be less than 1, since the model can flag a question as unanswerable. Similarly, letaARi and
eARi be the probabilities of producing correct or incorrect answer in AR after exactly i retrieval requests. Here,
aARi +e ARi may also be less than 1, as the model can continue to issue more retrievals instead of answering.
Throughout this analysis, we assume that the outcomes of each retrieval step are independent; that is, the
probability of any outcome at step i does not depend on the outcomes of previous steps. Therefore, the
accuracy of NR is simplya NR, and the accuracy of AR is given by
NX
