1 Introduction
The task of legal statute prediction [1–3] has been an active research area in recent
times. In this task, a case description (detailing the facts about the case) is given
as input and a set of relevant statutes to the case is expected as an output. In this
paper, we use the termstatuteto refer to a section, a sub-section, or an article of any
specific Act (e.g.,Indian Penal Code, 1860) or convention (e.g.,European Convention
on Human Rights). Table 1 shows some examples of statutes along with theirtextual
contents. Here, we use the termstatute contentfor the actual rule or regulation (textual
content) corresponding to a statute. Table 2 shows an example of a case description
along with a set of statutes relevant to that case.
