AoS model inference and explanation generation: The trained AoS model is
used for predicting relevant statutes for any new test instance, i.e., a new case descrip-
tion. The model also generates an explanation for each predicted statute in the form of
up toH(number of attention heads) sentences which correspond to the highest atten-
tion weights across all theHattention heads. Although, there has been some debate on
usefulness of attention for explanations in the literature [8, 9], we found it to be useful
in our evaluation (see the detailed evaluation of the explanations in Section 4.7). Mul-
