4.1.2 ECtHR B Dataset
This dataset consisting of the cases from The European Court of Human Rights
(ECtHR) was proposed by Chalkidis et al. [21]. It is also a part of the LexGLUE
benchmarks from legal language understanding in English proposed by Chalkidis et al.
[5]. ECtHR hears allegations that a state has breached human rights provisions of
the European Convention of Human Rights (ECHR). The dataset contains 11K cases
from the ECtHR public database. The cases were split chronologically into training
(2001–2016), development (2016–2017), and test (2017–2019) partitions. Table 6 pro-
