Most existing approaches for improving code
generation rely on supervised instruction tuning,
where LLMs are fine-tuned on curated problem-
solution pairs annotated by human experts or LLM-
based annotated. However, creating high-quality
instruction data requires substantial human effort
in problem design, implementation, and verifica-
tion, with costs increasing as model capabilities
advance. The recent (Yue et al.; Ye et al., 2025;
Chu et al., 2025) works emphasize that pre-training
brings the knowledge, and post-training is weak
at knowledge integration but focuses on knowl-
edge utilization and alignment.These challenges
motivate a fundamental question: Can LLMs au-
