their hand to reach significantly above the rim to actually slam the ball down. This typically requires the hand to be at least 10’6""
to 11’ above the ground (3.2 to 3.35 meters). Now, if an NBA player stands on the shoulders of an average person: The average
person’s shoulder height is roughly at their total height minus their head height, so about 5’4"" (1.63 meters) from the ground.
