long-document QA. Imperfect retrievers introduce noisy or even misleading evidence (Su et al.
(2024); Yoran et al. (2023); Khattab et al. (2023); Shi et al. (2023)), and generators (LLMs)
struggle to process very long inputs (An et al. (2024); Liu et al. (2023); Xu et al. (2023);
Li et al. (2024b)). As a result, answer quality often degrades as the corpus size increases.
