3.1.3 Manual Validation of the RoFlickr30k-QA Test Set
Since the questions and answers in RoFlickr30k-QA were synthetically generated, we could not correctly assess whether
the models would perform well on real-world human questions in Romanian. To address this, we manually corrected
the test split of the RoFlickr30k-QA dataset.
A single human annotator reviewed the 6,357 question-answer pairs and manually corrected the question and answer
fields. This validation focused on ensuring that each question was answerable from the image and that each answer
relied exclusively on visible visual information. The annotator corrected for grammatical and content errors, simplified
overly specific formulations when possible, and kept edits minimal. In addition, the answers were normalized to full
sentences.
