Table 4 summarizes the manual correction process for the RoFlickr30k-QA test set. The manual review affected a large
portion of the data, indicating that automatic generation required substantial post-processing. Most edits involved the
answer field, either alone or together with the question, reflecting the need to improve answer completeness, consistency,
and visual grounding. Question-only edits were comparatively less frequent, suggesting that the generated questions
were more stable than the answers.
Following prior work that uses CLIPScore to estimate image-text alignment [Hessel et al., 2021, Basnet et al., 2025],
we compute image-question and image-answer CLIPScores before and after manual correction. Formally, let Ii
denote an image from the dataset, X bi ∈ {Qbi , Abi } represent the generated question-answer text before correction, and
X ai ∈ {Qai , Aai }are the corresponding human-corrected versions. We thus define the correction gain as:
