ROUGE.Recall-Oriented Understudy for Gisting Evaluation (ROUGE) was introduced by Lin [2004] to address
the automatic evaluation of summaries. In this work, we use ROUGE-L, a variant based on the longest common
subsequence (LCS). More specifically, given a reference textR and a candidate textC, the longest common subsequence
LCS(R, C)is first computed. Based on the LCS , we derive the precision and recall (Equation 4), which are then
combined into the ROUGE-L F-score (Equation 5) using β= 1 . This corresponds to the harmonic mean of precision
and recall:
