BERTScore.BERTScore [Zhang et al., 2020] was proposed as an automatic method for evaluating text generation
tasks. It computes the similarity between a reference text R and a candidate text C by measuring the similarity of their
token-level contextual embeddings r∈R and c∈C , respectively. Firstly, token embeddings are generated with BERT
[Devlin et al., 2019], and then precision and recall (Equation 6) are computed based on the maximum cosine similarity
between token-embedding pairs. Finally, the F1 score is computed (Equation 7):
