For each prompt, the set of candidate answers is
divided into two subsets: the gold set, which includes
the ground-truth answers, and the surface set, which
includes all possible answers across all subjects. For
each candidate in the surface set, the model’s logits
are computed, and the logarithmic probability of the
first token is obtained and appended to the original
prompt. Then, the prompt is iteratively updated by
concatenating the previously scored tokens, and the
probability of the next token is calculated with respect
to this new prompt. This process continues until all the
tokens of the candidate are evaluated. The cumulative
