from an RRS-initialized SFT checkpoint places the policy
closer to a good solution, which complements the ablation
result that removing RRS leads to a noticeable drop in final
performance. Together, these observations justify RRS as
a key component for obtaining stable and high-performing
RL training in KBQA-R1.
