Key Insight.This case study illustrates thatgrounded environment feedback is the decisive factor. Without it, KBQA-
o1’s MCTS search is “flying blind”—the policy model generates plausible-looking action sequences, but neither the policy
nor the reward model ever observes actual KB execution results. This makes errors like wrong relation directions impossible
to detect. KBQA-R1’s multi-turn interaction paradigm enables genuine closed-loop reasoning that is both more accurate and
dramatically more efficient.
