Results.Metric-Fair Prompting with Qwen3-14B improves accuracy from 68% (single-item) to
84% (two-item, metric-fair, joint inference), demonstrating that coupling similar items via a fairness-
aware, margin-oriented protocol yields substantial gains on near-boundary decisions and promotes
cross-item consistency.
4.1 Qualitative Examples
We illustrate how Metric-Fair Prompting enforces cross-item consistency and fairness on three
highly similar question pairs selected by cosine similarity of stem embeddings (Qwen3-4B). In each
case, the model reads both items jointly, extracts decisive clinical/statistical features, and applies a
margin-based decision with a Lipschitz-like stability constraint.
