(b) project each item to the appropriate decision subspace (interpretation vs. method); and (c) preserve
cross-itemconsistency(e.g., larger n⇒ smaller SE; appropriate test tied to design/assumptions). The
pairwise setting reduces near-boundary errors that arise when interpreting an abstract in isolation.
