C Analysis on COT
As mentioned in §3.3, COT does not improve much
compared to DIRECTPROMPTING. In this section
we analyze in detail why COT can not improve
much.
Table 6 shows that the reasoning focus of DI-
RECTPROMPTINGand COT is quite similar, even
though COT organizes the reasoning into several
sub-points. While extensive research has demon-
strated that COT is particularly effective for com-
plex tasks requiring multi-step reasoning, such as
solving math problems (Wei et al., 2022), our task
(1)does not involve clear hierarchical reasoning
steps. As a result, the outputs of DIRECTPROMPT-
INGand COT are largely comparable;(2)the tested
LLMs struggle to autonomously construct effec-
tive reasoning processes for user simulation tasks.
For example, although LLMs can break the task
into steps likeunderstanding the statementand
personal context, they fail to fully integrate all de-
mographic information—such assex—into their
reasoning or determine the relative importance of
each feature.
