inspiration from Min et al., with their FACTScore approach,
which has been demonstrated in the literature to improve
correlation with human judgement compared to long-form
comparison [32]. This contrasts the ”Full” approach, whereby
the LLM judgement is produced to cover all summarised
points. Additional metrics were trialed for the graph-based
approaches, with graphs being generated for each dialogue turn
(to be evaluated in a pairwise manner with both the transcript,
as well as the ground truth summaries), as well as graphs
being evaluated using the full transcript graph. Additionally,
metrics have been calculated using the full dialogue transcript
for the LLM and graph-based metrics - due to their capability
in assessing long-form text.
