Figure 1.Overview. We employ specialized LoRA adapters to enable small (vision) language models to perform memory operations for
on-device deployment. The base model dynamically switches between expert adapters, each trained for a distinct stage: (1)knowledge
extraction, (2)memory update, (3)memory-augmented generation. In the last stage, the model can switch betweentext-onlyandmultimodal
adapter, depending on the input. By specializing each adapter for its specific operation, MemLoRA(-V) achieves performance comparable
