3.2SchED: SCHEDULE-BASEDEARLYDECODING
We proposeSchED, a confidence- and progress-aware early–exit algorithm for diffusion decoding.
At each step,SchEDthresholds the model’s aggregated token confidence against a smooth, nonin-
creasing function of progressp, i.e.,(¯g t ≥τ(p)). This design builds on the assumption that per-
token confidence typically rises as denoising proceeds, allowing generation to terminate precisely
4
