VI. PROMPTDESIGNSTRATEGY
We design prompts to maximize zero/few-shot performance
viainstructional scaffolding,knowledge contextualization, and
safety guidance. Figure 3 outlines the full template stack.
Fig. 3. The comprehensive prompt design strategy.
•Instructional Prompts: State the task and constraints in
plain language, e.g., “You are a digital assistant helping
elderly users with government services. Answer clearly
and safely.”
•Knowledge Injection Prompts: Prepend retrieved
knowledge{k 1, . . . , kN }in a fixed segment:
[KNOWLEDGE]:k 1 <SEP>k 2 <SEP>. . .<SEP>
kN
