• Timeout and Rate Limiting Issues.Retrieval failures can also arise from system-level constraints, including network
latency, high request volume, or temporary API throttling. These conditions may trigger timeouts, preventing content
from being returned within the evaluation. As shown in the table below, successive versions exhibited only minor
changes, and Krippendorff’s Alpha steadily increased across iterations.
