A. STREAM GAZE Data Construction Details
In this section, we elaborate details about STREAM GAZE
data construction pipeline. We first introduce details of gaze
projection (Appendix A.1) during preprocessing Sec. 3.1 and
fixation extraction (Appendix A.2). Then, we introduce ob-
ject extraction details with prompt (Appendix A.3) and QA
generation details by each task (Appendix A.4). Finally, we
introduce human annotation process details (Appendix A.5).
We also provide the full data construction procedure in Al-
gorithm 1.
A.1. Gaze Projection
To obtain frame-level gaze positions on the egocentric RGB
video, we convert each 3D gaze ray into a 2D pixel coor-
dinate using camera poses and calibrated intrinsics for the
HoloAssist dataset [27]. This method follows the hand–eye
projection procedure implemented in official code. 1 Each
gaze sample provides a world-coordinate origin o(t) and
direction d(t), while the camera stream provides per-frame
extrinsic matrices and intrinsics.
