Algorithm 2Threshold calibration viaLECfor single-model selective prediction with selection-conditioned error control
1:Input:G (a),{(x i, y∗i ,ˆy(a)i )}Ni=1,U,A,α
2:Output:Calibrated threshold ˆλ(a)
3:Compute uncertainty scores and error indicators for alli∈[N]:u (a)i ← U(xi;G (a)), err(a)i ←1{A(y ∗i ,ˆy(a)i ) = 0};
4: Sort uncertainty scores in ascending order u(a)(1) ≤ · · · ≤u(a)(N) , with corresponding error indicators err(a)(1) , . . . , err(a)(N) ;
5:Define candidate setT (a) ← {u(a)(1), . . . , u(a)(N) };
6:Initialize ˆλ(a) ←NULL;
7:foreachλ∈ T (a) do
8:Obtain selection indicators for alli∈[N]:S (a)i (λ)←1{u (a)i ≤λ};
9:Obtain joint indicators for alli∈[N]:Z (a)i (λ)←S (a)i (λ)·err (a)i ;
10:Compute the empirical linear constraint:L(λ)← PNi=1 Z (a)i (λ)−αS (a)i (λ);
11:ifL(λ)≤ −1then
12:Update ˆλ(a) ←λ;
13:end if
14:end for
15:if ˆλ(a) =NULLthen
16:Return“No feasible threshold for risk levelα”;
17:else
18:Return ˆλ(a);
19:end if
