1:Input:Models(G (a),G (b)), calibration set{(u (a)i , u(b)i , err(a)i , err(b)i )}Ni=1, risk levelα
2:Output:Calibrated threshold pair( ˆλ(a), ˆλ(b))
3:Sort{u (a)i }Ni=1 in ascending order and define candidate setT (a) ← {u(a)(1), . . . , u(a)(N) };
4:Sort{u (b)i }Ni=1 in ascending order and define candidate setT (b) ← {u(b)(1), . . . , u(b)(N) };
5:Initialize feasible setΛ (a,b)α ← ∅;
6:foreachλ (a) ∈ T(a) do
7:foreachλ (b) ∈ T(b) do
8:Obtain system-level selection indicators:S i(λ(a), λ(b))←1{u (a)i ≤λ (a)}+1{u (a)i > λ(a) ∧u (b)i ≤λ (b)};
9: Obtain system-level joint indicators: Zi(λ(a), λ(b))←1{u (a)i ≤λ (a) ∧err (a)i = 1}+1{u (a)i > λ(a) ∧u (b)i ≤
λ(b) ∧err (b)i = 1};
10:Compute the system-level empirical linear constraint:L(λ (a), λ(b))← PNi=1 ␀Zi(λ(a), λ(b))−αS i(λ(a), λ(b));
11:ifL(λ (a), λ(b))≤ −1then
12:Add(λ (a), λ(b))toΛ (a,b)α ;
13:end if
14:end for
15:end for
16:ifΛ (a,b)α =∅then
17:Return“No feasible threshold pair for risk levelα”;
18:else
19: Select the retention-maximizing feasible threshold pair: (ˆλ(a), ˆλ(b))←argmax (λ(a),λ(b))∈Λ(a,b)α PNi=1 Si(λ(a), λ(b));
20:Return( ˆλ(a), ˆλ(b)).
21:end if
When iterating over candidate thresholds, one can adopt binary search or other accelerated strategies. The search space can
be adjusted according to the specific UQ method, and finer threshold granularity can be achieved by decreasing the search
step size. All such procedures are performed offline during calibration; the test-time deployment remains fully real-time.
