4.1.2. Non-Traditional Academic Outputs
Figures 3 and 4 report graded evaluations for slide
and podcast tasks. In slide deck generation, GPT
models outperformed LLaMA in both papers, par-
ticularly in fluency, coherence, and correctness.
LLaMA only surpassed GPT in No hallucinations
and consistency for Paper 2, indicating better fac-
tual fidelity. In podcast generation, GPT again led
for Paper 1, excelling in engagingness and coher-
ence. However, LLaMA overtook GPT in Paper 2
across most dimensions, including reasoning and
completeness, suggesting higher adaptability to
certain texts.
