6.2 Generalization to unseen models
To further test the generalization of ORCA, we
compare Llama3.2-3B (Multi.) with Gemini-2.5-
Flash, training and evaluating for scenario B as
described in Section 5.1. This way, we ablate
ORCA’s generalization to LALMs that were pre-
viously unseen during training. As shown in Fig-
ure 3, ORCA outperforms Gemini on most un-
seen LALMs, notably on AudioReasoner, whose
responses generally have the highest variance in
human ratings, as it is the most verbose and dis-
tinct in response style out of all LALMs used in
this work.
