4.2. Implementation Details
Retrieval Details.To retrieve potentially informative docu-
ments for a query image, we employ EV A-CLIP-8B [48]. In
the coarse-grained stage, the entire query image is encoded
through EV A-CLIP to perform large-scale retrieval over the
knowledge base. For InfoSeek, we use an image-to-text
retrieval setup that computes similarity between the query
image and document metadata (i.e., the title of the page and
the summary). For Encyclopedic-VQA, we adopt image-to-
image retrieval, comparing the query image with the images
inside Wikipedia pages. In the fine-grained stage, we ex-
tract the main visual subject mentioned in the question using
the spaCy library4 and localize it in the image via Ground-
ingDINO [32], whose bounding box is re-encoded through
EV A-CLIP. Retrieval is done using the FAISS library [21],
with the top-kresults withk= 20retained at each stage.
Critic Model and Dataset.Independently from the genera-
tor scale, our critic model builds upon Qwen2.5-VL-3B, fine-
4https://github.com/explosion/spaCy
tuned on a curated subset of the ReflectiV A dataset [ 13]5.
The model is trained for 1 epoch with a learning rate of
2×10 −6 and a global batch size of32.
Generator Training.We build two versions of our gen-
erator, both based on Qwen2.5-VL [ 4], using the 3B and
7B model variants, and optimize them using the SFT plus
RL training scheme. In the SFT phase, we use the same
ReflectiV A [13] subset employed to train the critic model,
collecting reasoning traces from Qwen2.5-VL-7B. We set
α= 0.8 to give more importance to final-answer tokens.
The generator is trained for one epoch with SFT loss using
AdamW [ 34], a learning rate of 2×10 −6 and an effec-
tive batch size of 128. For RL post-training, we use the
full Encyclopedic-VQA and InfoSeek sets from ReflectiV A,
excluding samples from LLaV A-Instruct [31]. Each batch
includes 128 prompts with 8 completions per prompt. Train-
ing is conducted with Adam [22], a learning rate 1×10 −6.
Rewards weigh accuracy γ= 1.0 over format δ= 0.2 . In
all our experiments, we update the MLP adapter and LLM
weights while keeping the vision encoder frozen.
