mance of RAG-based approaches strongly depends on the
presence of the evidence passage in the retrieved set, and on
the number of passages provided to the generator.
In Fig. 3 (left), we evaluate the ability to produce the
correct answer when the evidence passage is either present
or absent in the context. ReAG consistently outperforms
all competitors of comparable scale, demonstrating that our
