Critic Threshold.In Fig. 8, we report how the performance
varies as a function of theyes-probability threshold used in
our critic model (cf. Eq. 4). The results show that instead of
simply letting the fine-tuned MLLM decide if the passage is
relevant or not (i.e., thresh= 0.5 ), leveraging the confidence
of the model in predicting the “Yes” token allows us to gain
more control over the filtering phase. A threshold thresh=
0.1 yields the best trade-off between precision and recall in
retrieving relevant passages. This setting enables the critic
model to reliably filter out passages for which it is most
confident of their non-relevance to the query.
Filtering Analysis.To evaluate the quality of our filtering
stage, we report passage-level statistics measuring evidence
retention (Recall) and irrelevant-passage recognition (Speci-
ficity) in Table 6. Our Critic retains relevant evidence with
higher recall while filtering irrelevant passages with higher
