bit-widths are allocated accordingly. The top thirty percent
most sensitive layers receive maximum bits (typically 8-bit),
the middle forty percent receive target bits (typically 6-bit),
and the bottom thirty percent least sensitive layers receive
minimum bits (typically 4-bit). Such adaptive allocation main-
tains overall quality while achieving higher compression than
uniform quantization.
