A Guessing on Benchmarks
Requiring consistency of correct answers on multiple,
independent answers to the same question of a bench-
mark is, intuitively, a way to assure that models which
are doing, to some extent, random guessing in a mul-
tiple choice benchmark. Here we explore the impact
of requirement consistency in M trials in terms of
determining minimum values for the guessing rate to
assure that a given consistency level is met.
We start considering a single multiple-choice ques-
tion q of k choices which is repeated evaluated by a
model M times, yielding answers llm(qi),1≤i≤
M, where llm(qi) = 1 if, and only if, the model
produces the correct alternative.
