tokens) is roughly 10× larger than the per-step
effect and 3× larger than the full reduction when
increasing from 1 to 4 distractors. Concretely, if we
randomly sample one response from a 1-distractor
image and one from a 4-distractor image, the first
response is longer only 40% of the time—barely
