Abstract:To test the hypothesis that fast an-
terograde molecular motor proteins power the
slow axonal transport of neurofilaments (NFs),
we used homologous recombination to gener-
ate mice lacking the neuronal-specific conven-
tional kinesin heavy chain, KIF5A. Because
null KIF5A mutants die immediately after
birth, a synapsin-promoted Cre-recombinase
transgene was used to direct inactivation of
