sentiment weights into the sequence-to-sequence objective.
Specifically, each tokenx i is assigned a weightλ i that reflects its emotional importance. The
weight is computed as a normalized combination of the token-level IG attribution scoreΦ(x i)and
the sentence-level sentiment probabilityp(s)predicted by a sentiment prediction model, wherex i
belongs to sentences:
λi =σ(Φ(x i) +β p(s)),
whereΦ(x i)is the normalized IG score for tokenx i,p(s)∈(0,1)is the predicted sentiment prob-
ability for its containing sentences,βcontrols the influence ofp(s), andσ(·)maps the combined
score into(0,1).
The original sequence-to-sequence training objective is reformulated as a sentiment-weighted loss:
