Document: Animation is the process of making the illusion of motion and the illusion of change by means of the
rapid succession of sequential images that minimally differ from each other. The illusion—as in motion pictures in
general—is thought to rely on the phi phenomenon and beta movement, but the exact causes are still unclear. Tom and
