Now note that the posterior distribution is by definitioncon-
sistentwith the evidence that we condition on. Therefore,
any ˆzi,ˆyi drawn from π(· |xi, y⋆i ) must satisfy ˆyi =y ⋆i
almost surely. This implies that checking whether the gener-
ated answer matches the ground truth is theoretically equiv-
alent to enforcing the posterior distribution’s support. Thus,
even if one were to sample from a broader proposal distri-
bution, applying a consistency filter ensures that the update
