C. Ablations Studies
We experiment with various rejection sampling budgetsM∈ {1,3,5} in RS. In Figure 4, we show an example where the
accuracy clearly increases with M. This gain is due to increased data utilization. However, even with this improvement, RS
is less accurate than both PPS and STaR. In addition, its computation time is (in the worst-case) linear in M and thus M
times higher than that of PPS. We summarize the highest accuracies attained by all sampling schemes on HelpSteer2 dataset
in Table 3. In all cases, the accuracies ofPPSare higher than those of any rejection sampling scheme.
We further examine robustness to the conditioning prompt. We experiment with two variants of the hint in Figure 1. The
first is “The score of the response should be {conditioning}. Do not output the hint.”, and we denote the corresponding
algorithms by PPS2 and STaR2. The second is “The score of the response should be {conditioning}.”. The corresponding
algorithms are denoted by PPS3 and STaR3. We show plots for all prompts and HelpSteer2 coherence in Figure 5. While
the absolute accuracy of the new prompts decreases, the relative ranking of the sampling schemes remains unchanged,
