Peak Belief Penalty Details
To calculate the penalty for each trajectory, we take the token count of longest belief state in the trajectory,
subtract the mean over all trajectories in the batch, and apply scaling factorkPBP = 0.01. We only apply
peak belief penalties to trajectories which do create a valid belief state, so as not to reward generating empty
beliefs. In addition, we set the penalty to 0 if the length does not exceed a fixed threshold ofTmin = 400
tokens for either trajectory in the group, we do not normalize the lengths by the in-batch range, and we apply
the penalty after advantage normalization, such that as the belief states get shorter the penalty has a smaller
impact. We found this was important to avoid over-compressed beliefs which significantly harm performance.
27
We note that it might be more effective to account for how many steps the agent took when calculating
PBP, because longer belief states may be required to describe the information collected over more steps of
information gathering.
