Answer Extraction and Citations
To evaluate the quality of the generated answers, we perform an extensive labelling effort resulting in 983 claims and 1146
citations annotated for 130 questions with the help of 13 independent annotators. The agreement on Answer Relevance is
perfect among all of the annotators, whereas it was at 0.90 for Citation Precision and 0.81 for Citation Recall, as can be seen in
Supplementary Table S3.
Table 4 summarizes the system’s performance. We find that a large percentage 86,3% of the answers are deemed relevant. For
citation quality, a substantial portion of citations are found to be relevant or partially relevant, both in terms of precision and
recall. Specifically, for citation precision, 76,3% of citations are relevant and 5,93% are partially relevant, out of 1146 evaluated
11/18
