F Adaptive Boundary Selection
This appendix provides a formal specification of the adaptive boundary selection mechanism referenced
in Section 9.1.
Definitions and target rateCandidate boundaries correspond to between-message indices
i∈{1,...,T−1}, whereidenotes the position between messages(m i,m i+1).
LetC(t)denote the number of candidate positions processed up to timet, and letS(t)denote the
number of boundaries committed up to timet. The adaptive controller targets a boundaryselection
rate
ρ=E
[S(t)
C(t)
