3.2.2 A2: Agent Output Signaled Agent Adaptation
Unlike the A1 paradigm, where the adaptation signal is derived from tool-execution outcomes, the A2 paradigm
obtains its optimization signal from the agent’s own final output. For simplicity, the following description focuses
on a single-turn interaction; the multi-turn case extends naturally.
