3.2.3 T1: Agent-Agnostic Tool Adaptation
In the T1 paradigm, the agent A is kept fixed, and adaptation is applied to only the external tool set T . The setting
arises when the agent is a closed-source API (such as GPT, Claude, or Gemini) that cannot be fine-tuned, or when
the goal is to augment a fixed agent by training specialized tools such as retrievers, rerankers, planners, simulators,
or additional foundation models. In this sense, a “tool” in T1 primarily refers to a trainable model, regardless of
whether it is a traditional machine-learning model or a large-scale foundation model.
