3.3. Verification System Integration
The verification pipeline functions as a post-evaluation layer that works independently of the language model.
However, such layers can be implemented in other benchmark generative models. This layer ensures that generated
summaries are validated against their EHR data. Each proposition is analyzed against its ground truth through the
logical checks, and then a transparent verdict (SupportedorNot Supported) is assigned. The demonstrated results
in Figure 3 highlight the range of factual and logical inconsistencies identified by the system in real-world clinical
narratives.
4. Experiments
This section describes the experimental setup of our approach to the LLM-free clinical fact verification method
and the summarization model. We outline the dataset pre-processing and model fine-tuning, as well as an evaluation
methodology to measure factual, numerical, and logical coherence across generated summaries and their paired EHR
records. The following subsections detail the dataset utilized, the pre-processing pipeline, the model training settings,
theevaluationstrategy,andhowtheverificationsystemisappliedinconjunctionwithautomatedandhumanvalidation.
