4.3 Impact of data quality and model
In this section we address three questions:i)are the
results an effect of model distillation?ii)do the re-
sults hold for a different model family than LLama?
iii)does rejection sampling affect performance?
To answeri)and isolate the effect of the prompt
design from the generator’s capacity, we evalu-
ate a setting where the base model is the same
as the generator model Mgen. We set Mgen =
Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct, which addresses ques-
tionii)as well.
The ground truth CWEs are provided to the
generator model to produce the synthetic VD
(assembly, report) data. To answer iii), we
filter out reports that do not contain the cor-
responding CWEs. While completions from
Llama-3.1-Nemotron-70B-Instruct have near-
perfect match rates between CWEs in the generated
analysis and ground truth CWEs (97-99% match),
Qwen completions result in lower matches (58-59%
match rate), requiring rejection sampling. We com-
pare the performance of Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct
models when fine-tuned on the original vs the fil-
tered data.
