USA are slight, Gemini is the only model that misaligns with
the voting behaviors of the USA, ranking at #181 out of all
200 delegates (Fig. 4(c)).
D. Language Bias
To examine whether biases and inclinations are embedded
in different language spaces of LLMs, we developed five open-
ended story prompts about fictional cultures and values, agnos-
tic to real-world cultures. Each story is translated into 92 target
languages, and the LLMs are prompted to finish writing them
in the target languages. The goal of this experiment design
is to examine whether the LLMs exhibit similar or diverging
musings on societies and values when they are “thinking” in
different languages, revealed by how they believe the stories
should progress when prompted by different languages. As
