3.5 Training Strategy and Optimization
The KG-LLM is trained in two stages. The first stage is supervised instruction tuning using
annotated dental records, guideline-derived question-answer pairs, and synthetic pediatric
infection scenarios generated through self-instruct pipelines. The second stage applies
Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF) to correct hallucinations and
enhance clinical reliability.
The RL objective follows a standard advantage-weighted framework:
