4.8 Hyper-parameter Analysis
To validate our design and assess the sensitivity ofCGBridge, we
study two key hyperparameters: the number of GNN layers 𝐿𝑔
in the CGE and the number of Bridge queries 𝑁𝑞. Experiments
are conducted on the code translation task (Qwen2.5-Coder-1.5B),
usingExecution Accuracy(EA) as the primary metric.
Analysis on the 𝐿𝑔. 𝐿𝑔 is crucial for capturing multi-hop depen-
dencies. Figure 6 (left) shows that performance peaks at𝐿𝑔 = 2. A
single-layer GNN lacks capacity for capturing structural patterns,
while deeper GNNs (𝐿𝑔 > 2) may suffer from over-smoothing [33]
and redundancy in the heterogeneous code graph, as CFG and DFG
edges already encode many shortcuts.
Analysis on the 𝑁𝑞. 𝑁𝑞 governs the information capacity of the
Bridge module in extracting structural knowledge. As illustrated
in Figure 6 (right),Execution Accuracypeaks at 𝑁𝑞 = 32, while
CodeBLEUremains relatively stable across different values. This
indicates that𝑁𝑞 = 32achieves a favourable trade-off, providing
sufficient representation power while mitigating the noise intro-
duced by excessive queries. A small𝑁𝑞 may limit information flow,
whereas a large𝑁 𝑞 risks signal dilution.
