C. Experiment Setting
We designed a series of experiments to establish perfor-
mance baselines for both pipelines. As listed in Table II,
we utilized various LLMs as backbones. Additionally, we
experimented with combinations of encoder and decoder ar-
chitectures in the Embeddings Pipeline, guided by empirical
performance results.
For theContentspipeline, we employed the following
configurations: (a) Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting for
standard classification (C R), (b) fine-tuning the LLM (C RT),
(c) our proposed PICEPR algorithm (C PR), and (d) its two-
shot prompting variant (C PR2). On the other hand, for the
Embeddingspipeline, we explored: (a) standard LLM-based
classification (V R), (b) fine-tuning the encoder model (V RT),
(c) adopting an augmented dataset generated by a decoder
