Although LRPE incorporates a progress ratio, it
remains explicitly dependent on len. During train-
ing, this implies that the inputs are not invariant
to the target length. In particular, the same ratio
yields different encodings depending on whether
the expected sequence is long or short.
To empirically validate this hypothesis, we repro-
duced the LRPE method and scaled it to the BART-
L architecture on the CNN/DailyMail dataset. As
shown in Tables 11 and 12, LRPE yields less
stable results and does not reach the same level of
accuracy as PRE in our main experiments.
