Each leaf gist token ⟨GT⟩k is designated to summarize its preceding sub-segment sk, and theattention scope is restricted to its associated sub-segment and preceding leaf gist tokens. The process
involves initial uniform partitioning of X into segments Xi, followed by adaptive budget reallocation
(determining the number of sub-segments b′i within each Xi) using an information content score (Eq.
2) to define the final sub-segments sk and the placement of their corresponding ⟨GT⟩k. A dedicatedtoken,⟨GT⟩, is incorporated into the LLM’s vocabulary for this purpose.
