stays competitive only in short-form tasks.
In table-to-text summarization (SciGen), Align-
Score approaches 98% to 100% across all methods.
We infer that factual alignment is easily met be-
cause of the structured inputs. Explicit reasoning
methods, like SC and IR, lose faithfulness when
provided with 2-shot examples. In contrast, LRMs
either stay the same or show slight improvement.
Overall, LRMs with implicit reasoning produce the
most faithful summaries.
