memory in healthy people. These effects are important for doctors to consider when prescribing pregabalin, especially for people who will take it long-term to
manage chronic conditions.
Mistral Antiepileptic drugs (AEDs), used for treating seizures and certain types of chronic pain, can sometimes cause side effects like problems with thinking and
memory. These issues are important to consider since AEDs are often taken for long periods. Pregabalin is a relatively new AED that is widely used for seizures
and pain management, including in a condition called fibromyalgia. [.......]. Moreover, the volunteers who received pregabalin also reported more complaints on
the Portland Neurotoxicity Scale, a questionnaire used to assess neurotoxicity symptoms, meaning that they noticed more issues with their thinking and memory
(p < 0.01). In conclusion, taking pregabalin at conventional doses and titration for 12 weeks caused mild negative cognitive effects and neurotoxicity complaints
in healthy volunteers. This information is essential when selecting and monitoring long-term AED therapy. The study provides Class I evidence that pregabalin
