B LEACE as a Concept Erasure method
LEACEis a concept erasure technique (Belrose
et al., 2023) that modifies the representations of a
binary concept so that predicting that concept is as
good as random chance (50-50). Here, we refer to
such a concept as being politically inclined or not10.
LEACE is based on the same principles of linear
representation hypothesis (Mikolov et al., 2013;
Park et al., 2025), which states that high-level con-
cepts are represented linearly in the representation
space of models, as other concept removal methods
