In summary, vLLM [10] offers a measurable architectural advancement. Its improvements in latency (achieving a
mean latency of ≈1.7s) and time-to-first-token (averaging ≈0.17s), even under high load with 32 workers, translate
into superior efficiency, scalability, and responsiveness. These findings empirically substantiate the transition of the
