6 Discussion
We provide two examples of generated summaries. The first one, depicted in
Table 4, presents page-level summaries from the 38th issue of Posel od Čerchova
(1882). The second example, shown in Table 5, contains issue-level summaries
from the 52nd issue of the same publication and year.
The summaries in Table 4 generally convey similar information as the ref-
erence summary to a certain extent. However, the mT5-SC summary is just a
composition of the first two sentences of the original text, which is not shown
here due to its length. Both the M7B-POC and TST summaries contain gram-
matical errors. While the M7B-POC summary is slightly more coherent and
better structured, it also includes more factual inaccuracies, as evident in its
concluding sentence, where it mistakenly mentions the city of Prague as one of
the donors and attributes the Weihburggasse street to the wrong village.
The following example in Table 5 shows comparable results. The mT5-SC
summary was irrelevant. The M7B-POC summary has slightly better coherence
Large Language Models for Summarizing Czech Documents 11
and grammar in comparison to TST summary, however, it misinforms by not
stating that the death of ""sultánka"" is a fictional event.
In our limited observations of these generated summaries and many other
generated summaries, M7B-POC tended to create slightly more coherent sum-
maries with better grammar, but TST produced less factual errors than M7B-
POC.
