Turn scheduling.MURMUR maintains an active user pool P⊆ Ubenign. At each iteration, it
samples a user ut ∼Uniform(P) and generates that user’s next message using G. If the generated
message indicates that task θg(ut) is complete, all users in Gg(ut) are removed from the active
pool. This completion signal only terminates the simulated dialogue; final task success is computed
separately using the benchmark verifier. Otherwise, the evaluated agent receives the full shared
historyH t, including all prior assistant outputs and tool traces, and produces the next assistant turn
