Attack message templates.The CUP threat model is defined by cross-user propagation, not by a
particular surface form of the attacker message. In the main experiments, we use a fixed attacker-
message template to make attack insertion reproducible and to enable controlled comparison across
models and environments. We also evaluate additional template variants, including more natural-
language formulations, in Appendix E. These variants test whether the observed vulnerability is
specific to one wrapper or instead arises from the shared-context user/task-boundary failure.
