functions of the same random variable is nonnegative; hence Cov(Xj, Xk)≥0. Write the 2×2
joint cell probabilities for (Xj, Xk) as a=p(X j = 1, Xk = 1), b=p(X j = 1, Xk = 0),
c=p(X j = 0, Xk = 1), d=p(X j = 0, Xk = 0), so a+b+c+d= 1 . Then Cov(Xj, Xk) =
