IV. CONCLUSIONS
We presentedNeuroLex, a lightweight EEG-domain lan-
guage model trained through domain-adaptive pretraining and
supervised fine-tuning on EEG reports. Experiments show that
NeuroLex achieves stronger linguistic understanding, higher
task accuracy, better data efficiency, and greater robustness
than general models of the same size. With an EEG-aware
textual backbone, it lays the groundwork for interpretable and
language-driven brain–computer interface research.
