generally yields optimal performance. While for summa-
rization, slightly longerLprove more suitable, emphasizing
semantic coherence through wider context capture. Regard-
ingc, we find that model performance is most stable and op-
timal whenc∈[1.0,2.0], balancing the trade-off between
exploration of uncertain paths and exploitation of known
high-return branches. Extremely small values ofclead to
