We measure how useful the automated clustering is by entity-
swap experiments: for a (source, target) pair we ablate
features from the source state and amplify the corresponding
features from the target state, and check whether the model’s
predicted capital is redirected to the target’s capital. Because
the only human-labeled graph available is the Dallas one,
every swap uses Dallas as target and one of the other 49
states as source; the target supernodes come from the human
annotation, while the source supernodes always come from
the auto pipeline (no human annotation exists for the other
49 graphs). Across the 49 sources, our supernodes redirect
the prediction to the target capital on40/49sources versus
38/49 for the human-labeled supernodes and 0/49 for the
random control; the top-K node-influence baseline saturates
at6/49when given∼100 features per call (Figure 4).
