4 GRAPH-OF-THOUGHTSBEHAVIORREASONINGSYSTEM
To explain conversational behavior rationales, we construct a Graph-of-Thoughts (GoT) (Besta et al.,
2024) that performs causal inference over predicted speech acts. Each behavior is represented as a
node in a directed graph with edges denoting causal relationships, allowing the system to score
behavior chains and provide interpretable rationales.
