4.2 SYSTEMDESCRIPTION
Given audio inputX={x t}Tt=1, we process 1-second segments using a causal window ˆUi of
sizeW= 30s. For each timestepi, we extract text nodesV texti (subject-relation-object triples
from incremental ASR using OpenIE) and speech-act nodesV sai (predicted high/low-level labels
(ℓhii , ℓloi )). The complete graphG i = (Vi,A i)combines both node types with adjacency matrixA i
encoding co-occurrence relationships. We encode the multimodal context using frozen encoders:
HuBERT (Hsu et al., 2021) for audio (h ai ∈R d), T5 (Raffel et al., 2020) for text (h ti ∈R d), and
GAT (Chen & Yang, 2021) for graphs (h gi ∈R d). Features are fused via gating and processed
by a causal Transformer to produce contextual representationsz i. More details can be checked in
Appendix A.4.
