A.9.4 NOISE ANDOVERLAPRATIOS
The ECDF 0indicates a broad SNR coverage (p10≈23 dB, p50≈33 dB, p90≈41 dB), with a
modest low-SNR tail. The corpus is neither overly clean nor dominated by noisy outliers. Overlap
ratios are strongly left-skewed (mode<2%, long tail up to≈22%), consistent with brief, sup-
portive overlaps rather than sustained interruptions. Noise primarily affects gap formation rather
than overlap intensity, while overlap appears more tied to prosodic activity; we therefore stratify
evaluation by SNR bins and supplement high-overlap slices for robustness.
