els. Higher rewards indicate messages that make
the session appear more realistic.
Preference Dataset Generation:For 2 mes-
sages with the lowest rewards, we sample 8 alter-
native responses. These alternatives are ranked by
their discriminator-based rewards to create pref-
erence pairs (uchosen, urejected) where the chosen
response has the highest reward.
Dataset Filtering:After generating prefer-
ence pairs, we filter to retain only samples where
rchosen >0 and rrejected <0 . This selects high-
confidence pairs with maximum learning signal
while preventing over-correction.
DPO Update:We train the new simulator using
DPO, which directly optimizes the policy to prefer
higher-reward responses. We use the previous itera-
tion’s simulator as the reference policy πref. Defin-
ing the implicit reward rθ(h, c, u) = logπθ(u|h,c)πref(u|h,c),the DPO loss is:
