B.2 MAUVE Configuration
MAUVE scores are computed using mauve-text4.
Utterances are embedded with OpenAI’s text-
embedding-3-small model, quantized into k= 250
clusters via k-means, and the divergence frontier
area is computed following Pillutla et al. (2021).
For the mental health domain, all user utterances
from a simulator’s sessions form distribution P ,
while all real user utterances form distribution Q.
The same procedure is applied to MultiWOZ ex-
periments using user utterances from the test set as
Q.
B.3 User Action Distributions
Figure 4 compares user action distributions across
simulators. For negative indicators (left), zero-shot
models dramatically underestimate rates of chal-
lenging behaviors: GPT-4o shows near-zero “Ag-
gressive to Chatbot”, and all base models under-
represent “Chatbot Loses User” and “Disagrees
with Chatbot.” This confirms that zero-shot models
produce unrealistically compliant users.
