C Additional Analysis on Filtering, Annotation, Data Standardization
and Generation Evaluation
C.1 Filtering and Data Annotation
To further clarify the role of DeepSeek in benchmark construction, we conducted two additional analyses
evaluating its effectiveness during the preliminary filtering stage.
First, we randomly sampled 150 pairs that DeepSeek filtered out and asked three human annotators to
manually review them. More than 90% of these pairs contained clear issues such as broken context, logical
contradictions, or severe incoherence. Only 3 pairs (2%) were considered potentially suitable for inclusion in
the benchmark. This confirms that the vast majority of DeepSeek-filtered pairs do not require additional
human inspection.
