achieves the best C score. Conversely, in the
MPChat dataset, the [E] model achieves the best
results in R@1 and MRR. The [N, E] model, which
beneﬁts from the LM loss during relation learning,
demonstrates the highest F1 but the lowest perfor-
mance in R@1 and MRR. The [none] model, on the
other hand, achieves the best C score. Addition-
ally, MoCoRP consistently demonstrates higher
PPL compared to BART.
