D Sensitivity Analysis
D.1 Impact of Base Decay Temperature
The parameter τfixed dictates the temporal hori-
zon of the alignment. We evaluated τfixed ∈
{2,4,8,16,32} on the MSC dataset. As illustrated
in Figure 2, we observe a clear concave trend:
• Small τfixed (Myopic):At τfixed, the model
aggressively suppresses history (54.2% win
rate) but loses coherence across sessions due
to contextual myopia.
• Large τfixed (Inertia):At τfixed, the decay
becomes negligible. The performance de-
grades significantly (51.2%), approaching the
TiDPO-DKL baseline (48.0%) as the model
fails to overcome inertia.
• Optimal τfixed:This setting strikes the equi-
librium, achieving the peak win rate of 54.9%.
