D.2 Impact of Bias Intensity
The parameter λ controls the aggressiveness of the
bias. We evaluated λ∈ {0.1,0.3,0.5,0.7,0.9} .
Figure 3 reveals anon-monotonic trendcharacter-
ized by a stability peak followed by a pathological
rebound.
• Optimal Region ( λ= 0.5 ):Provides suffi-
cient penalty to disrupt inertia without erasing
valid context.
• Over-correction (λ= 0.7 ):Excessive bias
suppresses non-conflicting history, damaging
general performance (51.3%).
• Myopic Rebound ( λ= 0.9 ):A patholog-
ical local optimum where the model treats
the context as empty. While this yields a
high conflict resolution win rate by default-
ing to the user’s latest prompt (exploiting the
28
judge’s recency bias), it theoretically compro-
mises the model’s ability to perform retrieval-
augmented generation.
