E.1 Inference Efficiency and Latency Analysis
(Dynamic Mode)
While our recommendedStatic Modeincurs zero
additional inference latency (as the bias is internal-
ized), users opting forDynamic Modeto handle
highly volatile contexts incur a marginal cost. We
clarify that this calculation does not bottleneck the
generation process due to the fundamental separa-
tion of theprefillanddecodingphases:
• Prefill Phase:The semantic conflict score
τ(u T ) is computedonce per turn. This in-
troduces a marginal increase in Time-to-First-
Token (TTFT) of approximately 15–20ms.
• Decoding Phase:During autoregressive gen-
eration, the bias matrix B remains static with
respect to the turn distance. Therefore, the
Inter-Token Latency (ITL) remains virtu-
ally identicalto the base model.
