B. Analysis of LLM Evaluations on Human Response Tiers
Figure 6 illustrates the scatter plots of human vs LLM evaluations, specifically for the human-rated High, Mid, and Low-tier
responses. As mentioned in the RQ2 section of the main text, these plots show that while the human-rated tiers form a clear
gradation, the LLMs tend to assign high scores more generally across these tiers. This visually confirms that the LLMs’ ability
to correctly rank the responses by quality is limited.
