C Hyperparameter Settings
Table 7 details the hyperparameter configurations. Across all set-
tings, we employ USNID as PTE(·) and GPT-4o-Mini as LLM(·) . We
use fixed parameters for DCS and HSR: |S𝑘|= 10,𝛿= 10, and
𝐾nbr = 10. For brevity, these constant values are omitted from the
main hyperparameter table.
We can observe that MMR proves to be the most effective choice
in the majority of cases. Notably, for the semi-supervised experi-
ments on the BANKING and CLINC datasets, we opt for a similarity-
based mapping strategy instead of one reliant on the LLM. This is
because these datasets feature a large number of known intents
(over a hundred). The LLM struggles to fully comprehend and ac-
curately map such a wide range of intents while strictly adhering
to the required output format. Consequently, a direct similarity-
based mapping provides a more robust and effective solution in
high-cardinality scenarios.
