D. Dataset Insights
AskEP blogs.Each expert-written answer from the AskEP blog entry comprises mul-
tiple sections (mean=3.89, maximum=9) (Figure 2a). Answer sections vary widely,
with an average of 155 tokens and a maximum of 772 words, indicating heterogeneity in
information granularity (Figure 2b). The ratio between question length and total answer
length averages 0.036, confirming that questions are short entry points while answers
introduce substantially more information (Figure 2c). User questions average 18 words,
consistent with concise layperson queries (Figure 2d). Answers have poor readability for
non-experts, with an average Flesch Reading Ease score of 26.2 (Figure 2e), suggesting
that proactive dialogue support is necessary for accessibility.
EUDial Dialogue Dataset.Dialogues average 4.3 turns (min=2, max=18). Fig-
ure 3a shows the distribution, confirming that most dialogues fall between 6 and 12 turns.
By role, citizen utterances average 12.0 words, and system answers average 39.7 words.
Figure 3b highlights the distribution of system answers. Pairing each citizen turn with
the subsequent EPRS yields a dialogue-levelq→aratio distribution with mean=0.311
(reflecting tighter, incremental exchanges compared to static QA pairs). Figure 3c il-
lustrates the distribution across dialogues. Measured with Flesch Reading Ease (FRE),
FRE averages 23.95 per turn; when averaged per dialogue, the mean per-dialogue FRE is
23.89, placing them in a difficult-to-read range for laypersons. Figure 3d shows the FRE
score distribution across answers.
