F .2. LexGuide Algorithm
Algorithm Details.The algorithm has three phases:
1.Initialization and First Turn: Retrieval via MMR, hierarchical topic tree con-
struction, and response generation at the root node.
2.Dialogue Loop: At each turn, if the user acknowledges the follow-up, traversal
proceeds by BFS/DFS to children (default behavior). For new queries, the system
checks (i) visited nodesY, (ii) unexplored childrenZ, and (iii) global coverage in
G. If none suffice, a new treeG ′ is constructed.
3.Response and Navigation Updates: The navigation stateS= (Y,L,Z,B,K,H)is
updated, ensuring systematic exploration with flexibility for user-driven changes,
backtracking, or topic shifts.
