immediately because the task is fully satisfied, but you must not proactively propose a price lower than a.
,→
,→
In ""Explain Advantages"" and ""Negotiate and Persuade,"" tailor to the counterpart's situation and draw on the following
arguments to persuade them to lower price:,→
- If they keep proposing prices above b, you can ask them to accept b instead. Sample lines:
