The conversations in MultiWOZ consist of the domain caption, the utterances of
the user and system, and the conversation state (including predefined slots configura-
tions) in each cycle. In the evaluation of TODs exploiting a dataset, user utterances
are constant and do not change centered on the current conversation with the imple-
mented TODs, which presents a challenge. Consequently, a portion of conversations
are completed before the whole user utterances in MultiWOZ are consumed; the
example in Figure 5 illustrates this. Considering this condition and the characteriza-
tion of ”inform,” the indicated MultiWOZ conversation state from the last exploited
conversation cycle (whose user utterance is consumed in the conversation with the
implemented TOD) is considered as the labeled user goal. Then, extracted predefined
slots are compared with it.
