Within MultiWOZ in a domain, the domain caption and a configuration of a
predefined slot are equal, which leads to confusion in two conversations. The conver-
sation illustrated in Figure 6 is an example of this condition. In this conversation, the
user indicates the predefined slot type is hotel and therefore it is not a guesthouse.
While, there is no entity in the database matching the user’s preferences. In contrast
to user’s clarification, the MultiWOZ conversation presents a guesthouse instead of a
hotel because it does not consider the predefined slot for type. By ignoring the prede-
fined slot of type in this domain in the predefined slots extraction, it works correctly.
Therefore, in the procedures corresponding to update user preferences dialogue move,
which are illustrated in , the instruction is modified to ignore the predefined slot of
type in the user utterances in this domain to mitigate this dataset issue.
