In the conversation illustrated in Figure 7, there is an inconsistency between the
indicated configurations for predefined slots in the labeled goal of MultiWOZ and
the utterances in the conversation. The user initially inputs ”Cambridge to Bishops
Stortford” as the departure and destination, in order. While, in another utterance in
the middle of the conversation, the user indicates, ”I need to depart from Bishops
Stortford and go to Cambridge,” in this way changes the configurations of departure
and destination. In contrast, the MultiWOZ labeled goal does not portray this change,
and incorrectly maintains ”Cambridge” as the departure and ”Bishops Stortford” as
the destination, contrary to the user’s changed preferences in the conversation. In
this conversation, there is no issue with the implemented TOD; consequently it works
without any changes. While to evaluate conversation completion, the information of
the presented entity must be compared with the correct goal in the conversation, and
not an incorrectly labeled goal.
