entities centered on user preferences presented to the user, and there are no contradic-
tions between the characteristics of the presented entities with the correct current user
goal and the information state of the conversation, but also the whole information of
entire congruent entities to preferences in predefined slots is presented to the user in
an order indicated centered on the text part of preferences exploiting entity ranker.
This mechanism ensures that there is no drop in success compared to inform. In other
words, if the predefined slots in a conversation are correctly identified, while the prefer-
ences beyond predefined slots considered in indicating the order of presented entitles,
no information that must be conveyed to the user is omitted in the presented entities.
Without contradicting this point, the evaluation of the presented method indicates
not only complete inform but also complete success.
Comparing the inform of the presented method with those of previous works exposes
an improvement of at least 2.8 points over the maximum inform from prior models
(SFN) on the test dataset. In Figure 9, it is evident that the success of previous meth-
ods is consistently lower than their inform. Table 3 exhibits that the gap between
inform and success is different across models, ranging from about 1 point in the case
of LA V A to 10 points in AuGPT and Mars. The ProTOD is based on in-context
learning of LLMs. To improve proactivity, collecting entity information in ProTOD is
not limited to the database. In calculating inform in the ProTOD paper and conse-
quently in this paper, the presumption is that passing entities without contradiction
with preferences, even if the entity is not in the database, improves inform. While this
presumption to calculate inform in TODs is challenging.
The presented method improves the updated combined metric (which combines inform
32
and success), with an increase of circa 5.8 points over the maximum updatedcombined
of previous models (HDNO). The updated combined of LA V A is comparable with
HDNO, with a difference of about 6 points compared to the presented method. It must
be considered that the gap between inform and success of LA V A is the smallest, while
its success is the maximum in the investigated previous methods in the test dataset.
In contrast, updated combined of SFN, which its inform is maximum, is in a lower
position in investigated previous works due to a drop in success.
Compared to the performance of previous works, the presented method improves
inform by 2.8 points, success by 6.6 points, and updated combined by 5.8 points, with
no gap between inform and success. It is important to point out that the maximum
performances of the previous models correspond to different TODs—no individual
model in prior works excels in whole metrics. In a way that, in investigated previ-
ous works, the model with the maximum inform is not essentially the model with the
maximum success.
