ObjectiveThe training procedure for REVERT
closely follows standard LLM finetuning. We begin
by initializing REVERT with a pretrained LLM
and finetune it using cross-entropy loss on the next-
token prediction task, applied selectively to the
training data described above. Importantly, since
REVERT is not required to perform the reasoning
process itself, we compute the loss only within
the verbalization segments of each sequence. For
positions outside these verbalization segments, the
model is trained to predict a special ⟨con⟩ token,
signaling that it is still in the thinking mode.
Formally, let IVERBAL denote the set of token
positions within verbalization segments, the set
of token positions spanning from ⟨bov⟩ to ⟨eov⟩,
inclusive. Conversely, let ITHINK represent the set
of token positions outside IVERBAL , corresponding
to the tokens used for LLM reasoning. Then, the
total loss is
