As illustrated in Figure 7, the control behavior
changes after removing the Utterance Length fea-
ture. Specifically, utterance lengths tend to increase
across all levels of language proficiency, while the
controllability of Tree Depth improves for high
complexity levels (t= 0.8, t= 1.0) but decreases
for lower complexity levels ( t= 0.0 , t= 0.2 ,
t= 0.4 ). Interestingly, the controllability of the
Intermediate Word Ratio is diminished after remov-
ing the Utterance Length constraint.
