3.4 Dataset Distribution
Table 3 presents statistics for the PACT dataset. It
comprises 8,687 conversations, averaging 21.43
turns per conversation with length of conversations
varying from 8 to 24 turns. The dataset contains
11,522,261 tokens, averaging 61.87 tokens per turn,
indicating sufficiently long conversations with ex-
tended turn lengths, contributing to complex inter-
actions. Also, it exhibits rich lexical diversity, fea-
turing 116,974 unique words and 545,804 unique
bigrams. Figure 3 shows the distribution of conver-
sations across different personality profiles. The
usage frequency and proportions of each dialog
act are summarized in Table 4. All personality pro-
files and dialogue acts occur in sufficient frequency,
thereby ensuring a comprehensive representation of
realistic conversational scenarios and demonstrat-
ing their effective utilization in the dialogue gener-
ation process. Incorporating various ABN-specific
dialog acts enhances dialogue diversity and better
mirrors real-life interactions. Overall, our dataset
