2.3. Evaluation Metrics
We evaluate reply quality using a combination of subjective and
objective metrics. Specifically, we adopt the GPT-4o model as
a scoring system that rates responses on six dimensions, includ-
ing relevance, encouragement, simplicity, flexibility, practical-
ity, and creativity, each on a 1–10 scale, then averages the sub-
scores, resulting in the final subjective score. Simultaneously,
we compute the conditioned perplexity (c-PPL) to quantify how
well each reply aligns with the user request and conversation
context. Together, these two approaches provide a holistic view
of the quality of the system’s reply content.
Beyond reply quality, we define several objective met-
rics to assess real-time performance and interruption han-
