Observationally, the BLEU score measures n-
gram precision with a brevity penalty to ensure
fluency and accuracy, which might affect the fi-
nal results in case of the same semantic meaning
between the predicted answer and the reference
answer. Consequently, we execute another exper-
iment by using GPT scores (Zheng et al., 2023),
a metric that uses a very large LLM (e.g., GPT-
4o) serves as an evaluator to judge whether the
predicted answer shares the same semantics as the
reference answer, to evaluate the output of our pro-
posed approach. The results of this evaluation are
reported in Table 2. Accordingly, although the
BLEU score is lower (10.4 vs. 15.7), GPT-score
reflects better semantic accuracy.
