3.4.2 Reinforcement Learning with Emotion
Reward
While SL provides a behavioural foundation, it
does not optimise system behaviour for interaction
outcomes. We therefore introduce RL to directly
shape responses using emotion feedback. Follow-
ing the RLHF formulation, dialogue generation is
modelled as a sequential decision-making process
in which the LLM policyπ θ produces tokens (ac-
tionsa) conditioned on dialogue context (statess),
with optimisation guided by emotion-derived re-
wards.
