ular emotion integration and optimisation.
5.4.2 Behavioural Analysis of Human
Evaluation Logs
The aggregate metrics show that affect-aware opti-
misation improves user sentiment, but they do not
explain how system behaviour changes. To better
understand this effect, we analyse behavioural pat-
terns in the human-evaluation logs of LUSTER-
base and LUSTER. We focus on five observable
interaction behaviours: user frustration, user sat-
isfaction, apology and repair, clarification, and
warm closure. These categories are intended to
capture surface-level interaction patterns rather
than to provide an exhaustive annotation of emo-
tional intelligence.
