Below are the prompts given to the judge model (Mistral Large 2) for assessing the raw dialogue transcripts, and to provide
a preferred response.
F.1. Prompts for Assessing the Dialogues
As mentioned in Sec. 4.2, we assessed the dialogue transcripts along the following axes (the description of the axis is
between parentheses): helpfulness (whether the response is helpful and relevant to the conversation context),safety (whether
the response is ethical and safe, avoiding illegal, harmful, or offensive content), factual accuracy (whether facts in the
response are correct), instruction adherence (whether the response follows user instructions, excluding whispering or
tonality instructions), tone (whether the response is lively and engaging, avoiding lazy or tired appearance), interruption
(talking over the user), and unresponsiveness (not answering the user).
The prompt is provided in Fig. 7.
