C Implementation Details
BlenderBot is a dialogue model widely used for
generating emotional support response (Liu et al.,
2021; Zheng et al., 2023). We use the small ver-
sion of Blenderbot, training the model on ESConv
according to the code †.
MultiESC (Cheng et al., 2022) is a multi-turn
emotional support dialogue system that supports
strategy planning by capturing subtle emotional
expressions and emotional reasons, thereby antici-
pating user feedback and dynamically tracking the
user’s state. We use the released codes † to train
MultiESC on ESConv.
ESCoT (Zhang et al., 2024a) is an emotion-
focused, strategy-driven explainable dialogue sys-
tem. The system’s best model † is the Llama2-7B-
chat model trained on the ESD-CoT dataset, and
we conduct comparative experiments based on this
weight.
†https://github.com/thu-coai/Emotional-Support-
Conversation
†https://github.com/lwgkzl/MultiESC
†https://github.com/TeigenZhang/ESCoT
