For lexical diversity evaluation, we employ
three length-insensitive metrics: Moving Average
Type-Token Ratio (MATTR) (Covington and Mc-
Fall, 2010), Measure of Textual Lexical Diver-
sity (MTLD) (McCarthy, 2005), and Hypergeo-
metric Distribution Diversity (HD-D) (McCarthy
and Jarvis, 2010). For meaningful comparisons
across these metrics with different value ranges,
we develop a unified metric called the Lexical Di-
versity Score (LDS). The LDS formula, defined in
Equation (1), normalizes these three metrics to a
comparable scale through tangent transformation:
