Dialogue State Tracking (DST)As suggested
by Feng et al. (2023), LLM prompting shows
promising performance in DST, so we take a sim-
ilar prompting approach in this work. For each
slot, LLMGCG creates explicit instructions to ex-
tract the value from the entire conversation history.
We leverage Colang’s Natural Language Descrip-
tion (NLD) feature to execute these instructions
with LLMA and save the value to a slot variable.
Formally, a slot variable v(s)j ∈V (S) is predicted
as Equation 2, where p(s)j ∈P (s) is the prompt
generated by LLMGCG to extract the value for v(s)j .
