Interestingly, even smaller models like Qwen2.5-7B demonstrate reasonable performance (86.5%
relevance and 96.0% factuality). This robust performance across different model scales indicates that
the user simulation approach is feasible and practical even with more accessible open-source models.
The high performance across different model sizes validates the viability of using LLMs for user
simulation in legal consultation scenarios, making it a promising direction for developing and testing
legal consultation systems.
