We observe significant differences in entropy
distributions between distractor and on-topic in-
puts at layers 16 and 19 (Figures 3 and 6). While
both layers exhibit clear distributional differences,
the relative entropy values vary by layer; on-topic
inputs show higher entropy in some layers (Fig-
ure 3a), whereas distractor inputs have higher en-
tropy in others (Figure 3b). Notably, as seen in
Figures 3a and 3b, the distinction at layer 16 is
more pronounced. The implications of these dif-
ferences on experimental outcomes are discussed
in Section 5.2, while a detailed analysis of the ob-
served entropy patterns is provided in Section 6.4.
Based on these findings, we select layers 16 and 19
as L, where L represents the LLM layers used for
entropy extraction.
