A.1 Details for Patient-Centric Graph
The patient-centric graph contains a patient node, patient characteristics, and
medical information. For patient characteristics, we extract gender, age, blood
pressure, and pregnant state if mentioned in the dialogue. For medical informa-
tion, we mainly focus on the extraction of diseases, symptoms, and medications.
The disease and symptom have the following slots and values:
– state: [""patient claims positive"", ""patient claims negative"", ""doctor claims
positive"", ""doctor claims negative"", ""unknown""]
– past medical history: [""yes"", ""no"", ""unknown""]
The medication has the following slots and values:
– whether taken: [""yes"", ""no"", ""unknown""]
– whether effective: [""yes"", ""no"", ""unknown""]
– whether doctor recommend: [""yes"", ""no"", ""unknown""]
We further extract relevant information about the medical concepts as mem-
ory which does not belong to the above fields.
