A.2 Details for Medical Path Schema
The path schema used for generating path-based prompts is shown in Figure 5.
Our main idea is to acquire or exclude possible medications based on the medi-
cal condition of the patient. The subsequently constructed path-based prompts
18 Zhong et al.
which contain context-relevant knowledge can assist the medication recommen-
dation. We can also change the target from acquiring the treatments to suitable
food, medical tests, etc., therefore adapting the schema to fit the diagnostic
interviewing scenario.
A.3 Details for LLMs
We use ChatGPT-3.5-Turbo (version 1106) for the experiments. The prompts
we used in the experiments are shown in Table 4-8.
A.4 Details for Error Analysis
We pre-define 3 types of recommendation errors on DialMed. Following are the
definitions:
– Overlooking Medical Factors: the LLM provides a recommendation that
fits the symptoms but conflicts with some medical information mentioned in
the dialogue history. E.g., Loratadine for relieving itching during pregnancy.
– LackofKnowledgeaboutMedications :theLLMprovideswrongrecom-
mendations for the patient’s symptoms or disease. E.g., Bicyclol for treating
dizziness.
– Overlooking the Main Symptoms: the patient inquires about medica-
tions about one symptom, but the LLM focuses on another mentioned in the
dialogue, such as the past medical history of the patient.
