4.3.4 Active Learning-based Optimization. After pretraining, we
conduct online RL to further enhance the agent’s planning capacity
through exploration. We prompt three LLMs as the user, system,
and critic to perform self-play conversations. At each turn 𝑡, the
planner selects a dialogue strategy according to𝜋𝜃(𝑎𝑡|𝑠𝑡), guiding
the system LLM to generate a response𝑢𝑠𝑦𝑠𝑡 . The simulated user
then provides a reply𝑢𝑢𝑠𝑟𝑡 , and the critic evaluates the dialogue state
to assign a reward𝑟𝑡 for the strategy𝑎𝑡 . This process continues until
the dialogue goal is achieved or the maximum turn is reached. After
the interaction, we train the agent using a vanilla policy gradient
method following prior work. The formalization of this training
objective is as follows:
