6.2 Baselines
Several models have been introduced to improve multi-turn respon se selection.
Building on the work of [10], which utilizes CCA for feature extraction to iden-
tify intents and discourse tokens, this study extends that appro ach. In partic-
ular, it enhances response coherence by learning discourse token s with higher
correlations, thereby improving discourse-level understanding.
6.3 Result and Analysis
The performance of all baselines and our proposed model using Rec all is shown
in Table 1. It is evident from the table that the model signiﬁcantly out performs
all other models in terms of most of the metrics on the Ubuntu datas ets.
The insights derived from qualitative metrics reﬂect the quality of th e top-k
selected responses, as presented in Table 2. A lower perplexity sco re indicates
that the model more accurately predicts the data, demonstratin g a better un-
derstanding of the language. The BLEU and Rouge scores range fr om 0 to 1,
with a score of 1 representing a perfect match between the gener ated text and
the reference text. As shown in Table 2, the proposed model achie ves higher
translation quality and greater diversity in distinct unigrams and bigr ams. The
results clearly demonstrate that the model excels at retrieving co herent candi-
date responses and exhibits a stronger understanding of contex tual information.
