D3QN’s discount factor𝛾 to 0.9. For the KQR, we use a decay factor
(controls the smoothness of the kernel) of 0.9 for the ParentNet and
apply a QP solver [56] during training for the ChildNet.
5 Discussion of Results and Analyses
5.0.1 Predictions of the latent personality traits. TP3M takes as in-
put a one-turn utterance composed of state-action pair (𝑠𝑡−1,𝑎𝑡−1),
to predict the persuadee’s personality at time𝑡. We use five-fold
cross-validation to assess TP3M’s reliability to ensure its gener-
alizability to unseen data. The results are as follows: MSE=0.166,
RMSE=0.407, MAPE=0.092, R2=0.830, and MAE=0.254 3, which in-
dicate that TP3M performs well in minimizing prediction errors.
To further assess TP3M’s performance, we computed the top four
canonical correlation analysis (CCA) components of the ground-
truth OCEAN and TP3M’s estimated OCEAN values (Fig. 5). In-
terestingly, these top four CCA correlations exceed 0.96, which
indicates that analyzing the ongoing dialogue can reveal latent
personality factors closely tied to the persuadee’s personality.
5.0.2 Causal relations among utterance strategies. GRaSP discov-
ered 36 cause-effect pairs that are plausibly behind the utterance
strategies of EE and ER, where EE strategies serve as causes and ER
strategies as effects. A portion of the causal graph discovered by
GRaSP is shown in Fig. 6, which demonstrates interestingly how
various strategies used by EE could influence the strategies of ER.
Following are some key insights. (1) Prevalence oflogical appeal (18
cause-effect pairs): this strategy was predominantly used by ER in
response to EE’s positive-to-inquiry and task-related-inquiry strate-
gies. Our statistics show that 238 dialogues feature logical-appeal
and positive-to-inquiry strategies together, and 271 dialogues feature
logical-appeal and task-related-inquiry strategies. These highlight
logical appeal’s key role in addressing EE’s informational needs. (2)
Role of personal-related-inquiry (4 pairs): this strategy is frequently
used by ER following EE’s positive-to-inquiry and acknowledgment.
We find that 263 dialogues feature personal-related-inquiry and
positive-to-inquiry strategies together, and 172 dialogues feature
personal-related-inquiry and acknowledgment strategies, highlight-
ing the role of personal-related-inquiry in personalizing the dia-
logues. (3) Role of emotion-appeal (7 pairs): ER frequently employs
this strategy when responding to EE’snegative-to-inquiry strategies,
