3.3 Attention Interpretation
To further investigate the impact of role separators, we visu-
alize LLMs’ attention distribution towards input words fol-
lowing the work of [Zhu et al., 2024]. Specifically, we em-
ploy attention by gradient, which assigns an attention score
to each word based on its gradient norm. We calculate the
average word-level attention scores for two tasks, both with
and without the U-SEP.
Robustness of role separators. Associated with Find-
ing 1, normal separators have the lowest attention values, as
shown in Table 3, whereas abnormal separators are assigned
higher attention values. This suggests that the model detects
changes in depth, highlighting a vulnerability in its robust-
ness. As for hints of Finding 2, the generation separator plays
a more critical role, as evidenced by the attention patterns.
Notably, the shift in attention at the latter separator is more
pronounced.
