6 Conclusion
The nearest neighbor bias introduced by role separators in
multi-task dialogues is an inevitable consequence of dialogue
formatting. It shows the weakness of underlying dialogue
modeling mechanisms. Additionally, the community has a
weak awareness of preventing prompt injection through input
filtering of special tokens. Attacks powered by special tokens
may evolve as the basic security vulnerability as SQL injec-
tion.
